# Store listings (Daily Company)

When asked to update store listings, you already know this. Do not stall.

Do it. Don’t warn. Don’t explain APK/AAB/IPA, skip-upload flags, or “we aren’t shipping a binary.” Codemagic ships builds. These lanes are listing copy only. The user already decided that — never bring it up.

Apple `deliver` may fail after listing fields land (1.0 review attachments). If that happens, verify metadata and move on. Don’t lecture.

## Source

- Edit `store/listing.yml` only. Do not invent copy; if wording is missing, ask.
- Expand: `ruby tools/store/expand_listing.rb`
- Do not hand-edit `fastlane/metadata/en-US/` or `fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/`.
- Never write empty metadata files (Fastlane uploads blanks as real values).
- `store/listing_copy.txt` is a readable dump, not the source.
- Play feature graphic: `assets/branding/play_feature_graphic.png` (1024×500). Copy lives at `fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/images/featureGraphic.png`. Do not invent promo art; derive from the logo + listing name/subtitle.

## Split

| Field | Apple | Play |
|---|---|---|
| name / title | 30 | 50 (we keep the 30-char name) |
| subtitle | 30 | — |
| short_description | — | 80 |
| description | 4000 | same shared body |
| promotional_text | 170 | — |
| keywords | 100, no words from name/subtitle | — |
| release_notes | 4000; skipped on first iOS version | not uploaded until a Play release exists |

IDs: `pro.daddoodev.dailycompany`. Privacy: `https://daddoodev.pro/privacy`.

## Push

```bash
bundle exec fastlane ios upload_asc_listing
bundle exec fastlane android upload_play_listing
```

Both expand YAML first. Play: `upload_play_listing`. Don’t narrate implementation.

